tags: advisor
view-if: advisor_fatemi_available = 1 and advisor_fatemi_active = 1

= {!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Hossein Fatemi{!</span>!}

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Fatemi{!</span>!} is
a journalist who has joined the common election protest around
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}. His consultation
does not treat him as the sole editor of every friendly paper.

- @fatemi_message
- @fatemi_network
- @fatemi_dossier
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@fatemi_message
title: Sharpen the public message
subtitle: <span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">Fatemi</span> reduces the campaign to a line editors can carry from headline to meeting hall
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; press_coordination_timer = 0; press_project = "Fatemi editorial campaign"; press_project_stage += 1; press_capacity += 5; public_mandate += 3

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Fatemi{!</span>!} reduces the current case to a headline, a short explanation, and a set
of answers for predictable objections. Friendly editors adapt the brief to
their own papers rather than printing an identical instruction.

[? if front_formed = 0: The election protest speaks more clearly in public.
The participating papers and politicians remain independent, and arguments
that do not fit the chosen emphasis will need attention elsewhere. ?]
[? if front_formed = 1: The
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} speaks more
clearly in public. Arguments that do not fit the chosen emphasis will need
attention in a later cycle. ?]

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@fatemi_network
title: Coordinate friendly editors
subtitle: Independent papers coordinate timing and argument without becoming an official party press
view-if: front_formed = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; public_meetings_timer = 0; press_capacity += 4; organizational_reach += 2

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Fatemi{!</span>!} convenes editors to compare what they can verify, what readers are
asking, and which claims should not be repeated without evidence. The papers
remain independent, but their reporting no longer works at cross-purposes.

The network carries the campaign's arguments farther without turning friendly
papers into a single controlled organ.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@fatemi_dossier
title: Prepare a documented rebuttal
subtitle: The rebuttal sacrifices speed for a record opponents must answer point by point
view-if: front_formed = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; press_capacity += 3; constitutional_legitimacy += 3; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 2

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Fatemi{!</span>!} organizes a rebuttal around dated statements and institutional records,
marking uncertain reports instead of turning them into accusations. Editors
gain material they can quote and check over more than one issue.

The response is less dramatic than a single slogan, but it strengthens the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front's{!</span>!} claim to speak
from evidence and constitutional principle.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
